# early writes its free x before its own declaration: the first use resolves by the ordinary outer path (B26); the
# immediate caller is the root, so the write goes to the root's x (the book, #binding-caller-place). The later `int: x` starts
# an own place (book #binding-fallback: a shadowing event, not a repeat), filled by autofill from the root's x, now 7 (Р114):
# before_declaration 7 and outside 7. Until step 21.4 the row pinned outside 90 (the copy reading of 2026-11-18).
int: x 90
fn: tick () int (int: calls 0)
    calls := calls + 1
    return: calls
end: tick
fn: early () int
    x := 7
    int: x
    return: x
end: early
fn: local (int: a) int
    int: value tick()
    int: a
    a := a + 10
    return: value + a
end: local
int: before_declaration early()
int: first local(5)
int: second local(5)
int: calls tick\data\calls
int: stored local\data\value
int: outside x
